title: 'pallet-revive: keep an unreleased storage deposit refund refundable'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    On a runtime using `PGasDeposit`, a refund for removed contract storage is released only to the account that paid the deposit in native currency. When a different account removes that storage, the backend releases nothing, but the contract's recorded storage deposit was already lowered by the full refund. The unreleased amount stayed on hold and could only leave it at contract termination, paid to the terminating origin.

    The unreleased part is now added back to the contract's recorded storage deposit, so a later storage removal by an entitled account releases it. No migration is needed: deposits already stranded on existing contracts stay on hold until that contract is terminated.

    `Deposit::refund_on_hold` returns the amount released from the hold instead of `()`. Only the pallet's own backends implement the trait, which is sealed; callers of the method need to accept the new return type.

    `PGasDeposit::refund_all` returns the amount released from the contract's holds, including the burned part of the PGAS hold, as the trait documents. It returned the native part plus only the PGAS share credited to the destination. The storage deposit reported for a call that terminates a contract on a `PGasDeposit` runtime now includes the burned share. The amounts credited and burned do not change.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
